ight_house_break\n- When: 2025-01-18 03:33\n- Where: 9th Main Road, Kodambakkam\n- Vehicles: []\n- Described: 2 offenders, age 30-40, medium build\n- Weapon: cutter\n- MO: null\n- Visual tags: null\n\nDistance: 3.3 km\nDays apart: 1.0\nFactors: space_time (0.38), suspect_description (1.0), weapon_tool (1.0)\nScore: 0.733, band: medium\nCoverage: 0.35\n\nIssues:\n- MO is null on Crime B - cannot confirm same approach (cut_window_grille), escape (on_foot), etc.\n- Suspect description \"two males 30-40 medium build\" is very generic\n- Cutter is a common house-breaking tool\n- Coverage is low (0.35)\n- Different stations (PS-KUMARANNAGAR-R6 vs PS-KODAMBAKKAM-R2)\n- 3.3 km apart, 1 day apart - moderate spatiotemporal proximity\n- The score 0.733 is driven by perfect suspect_description and weapon_tool matches, but these are generic\n\nLooking at the prior vetted answers, I can see similar patterns. In the first prior answer, the Skeptic sent back a similar pair (CHN-KA-2025-000077|CHN-KU-2025-000078) with the same data, recommending send_back with a requery for narrower ring (2 km) and MO details.\n\nIn the third prior answer, the Skeptic sent back two pairs (CHN-KU-2025-000078|CHN-MG-2025-000077 and CHN-AS-2025-000080|CHN-KU-2025-000078) which had 1.3 km and 1.5 km distance, same night, but null MO on second crime.\n\nFor Pair 1 (CHN-KU-2025-000078|CHN-PO-2025-000068):\n- 2.3 km apart, 4 days apart\n- Same suspect description (generic: 2 males 30-40 medium build)\n- Same weapon (cutter - common house-breaking tool)\n- Null MO on Crime B\n- Low coverage (0.35)\n- Different stations\n\nFor Pair 2 (CHN-KA-2025-000077|CHN-KU-2025-000078):\n- 3.3 km apart, 1 day apart\n- Same suspect description (generic)\n- Same weapon (cutter)\n- Null MO on Crime B\n- Low coverage (0.35)\n- Different stations\n\nBoth pairs have the same issues: generic suspect description, common weapon, null MO on one crime, low coverage. The spatiotemporal proximity is moderate at best.\n\nI should send